# Storm, Windrider: "Creatures with flying can't attack you or block creatures you control" (CR 508.1c, 509.1b) and "Whenever
# you cast a spell that targets one or more creatures, those creatures gain flying until end of turn" (CR 603.2, 611.2a).
# On turn 3 Lightning Bolt at Bot2's face targets no creature, so nothing gains flying. Healing Salve on Memnite, then Giant
# Growth on the Grizzly Bears: each spell's own trigger gives flying to its own spell's target, the later first. Bot2 Mana Leaks the
# Giant Growth with its trigger still on the stack: the spell is gone but the Bears are still "those creatures" and gain flying, so
# the Bears have flying while the Memnite does not yet; the Memnite gets it from its own trigger after. Both are read on turn 4
# to have lost it: they attack Bot1, and Bot2's Ornithopter (flying all along) is refused. Storm (flying, untapped) blocks the
# Memnite, since the rule is only about blocking Bot1's creatures. On turn 5 Storm attacks and the Ornithopter may not block.

